// M5-A3P-1000. Ch17 B10 "The first lamp" (E, held input, 2 min, ~40 words). act3_ch17.md §2 B10.
// Morning, the hull's engine room. Liss and Rhen fit the Kite's first lamp the way they mended the Ch11 lamp: three
// held inputs (if ch11_lamp_repaired the rhythm is the same: the player's hands remember). THE LAMP IS BOUND LIGHT and
// Liss says so (§10 Q2 default): the Kite flies on the held dead. Nobody answers her. The glimmer is bound: still.
title: ch17_the_first_lamp
location: ch17/hollowmere
---
@camera D16
@music kite_first_lamp fade=2.0
@mark liss engine_bench walk
@mark rhen engine_bench_b walk
@wait 2.0
<<event hold_input hold_steady>>
@anim liss seat_burner_seat
@wait 3.0
<<event hold_input_end>>
<<event hold_input turn_collar>>
@anim liss turn_collar
@wait 3.0
<<event hold_input_end>>
<<event hold_input seat_it>>
@anim rhen seat lamp_housing
@wait 3.0
<<event hold_input_end>>
@vfx glimmer_bound at=kite_lamp count=1
@sfx lamp_seat
@camera D17
@wait 3.0
Liss [neutral]: That's bound light. Same as every lamp we ever made. #line:ch17_lamp_001
@wait 2.0
Liss [sad]: It'll fly on them. To let them go. #line:ch17_lamp_002
@wait 5.0
<<set $ch17_first_lamp_lit = true>>
===
